 "title": "Smart Devices Keep Dropping? Fix Your Wi-Fi First #shorts",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "Camera dropping offline? Doorbell slow? The problem usually isn't the device. It's the Wi-Fi."
  },
  {
   "text": "One router in a corner of the house can't reach the garage, the backyard, and the front door."
  },
  {
   "text": "A mesh system fixes that. Several nodes work together as one network, with one name and one password."
  },
  {
   "text": "Placement matters. Put each node in the open, about halfway between the router and the dead zone. Not in a closet, and not behind the TV."
  },
  {
   "text": "If you can, connect the nodes with an Ethernet cable. A wired backhaul is faster and more stable than wireless."
  },
  {
   "text": "And many smart home devices only connect on 2.4 gigahertz, so keep that band turned on."
  },
  {
   "text": "Strong Wi-Fi first, smart devices second. Free quote at novaprohome.com."
  }
